        <description> 
            The four Solar Array Wing (SAW) cameras are modified GoPro Hero 4 Black cameras hard-mounted 
            on the tips of the four solar array wings of the Artemis II Orion spacecraft. The SAW 
            cameras provide still and motion images during the mission for engineering and flight 
            operations and science observations. Due to its location and orientation of the spacecraft, 
            the SAW3 camera was the primary camera capturing still images and video of the Moon during 
            the lunar flyby.
        </description>
